
                                                  CONFIG SPLIT COMMAND


Config split command implements the split functionality

-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES               |    DESCRIPTION
-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -in_t               |    Template input XML file.
   -split_in           |    Input file for split.
   -out_t              |    Template output XML file.
   -split_out          |    Output file for Split.
   -rule_t             |    Template rules XML file.
   -split_rule         |    Rules XML file for split.
   -hex_split_in       |    Input HEX file for split.
   -hexmod_split_log   |    Log file for hexmod split.
   -hexmod18           |    To identify it is MDG1 project.
-----------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:

--split_func
--core_exp          _gen/swb/module/coreproc/filelist_gen_merged_exp.txt
--in_t              _gen/swb/module/hexmod/INPUT.XT
--split_in          _gen/swb/module/hexmod/data_input.xml
--rule_t            _gen/swb/module/hexmod/RULES.XT
--split_rule        _gen/swb/module/hexmod/data_rules.xml
--out_t             _gen/swb/module/hexmod/OUTPUT.XT
--split_out         _gen/swb/module/hexmod/data_output.xml
--hex_split_in      _bin/swb/R4Cx800xB.hex
--hex_split_out     _bin/swb/filegroup/results/R4Cx800xB_data.hex
--hexmod_split_log  _log/swb/module/hexmod/hexmod_data.log
--logfile           _log/swb/module/hexmod/config_hexmod_data.log
--hexmod18    
--lyt        0x10
	